ADT_STR CPU inference component

This component is adapted from pier-maker92/ADT_STR, version 1.0.0:
https://github.com/pier-maker92/ADT_STR/tree/77dbef225e7029478ebfb916f20c7a00274f0f12

The original work and this adapted component are licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-SA-4.0

Changes: inference-only CPU implementation for Python 3.14 and current
PyTorch; training/Hugging Face wrappers removed; explicit General MIDI
mapping, standalone JSON interface, bounded streaming input, progress,
owning-process checks, and grammar-constrained decoding added. The
decoder enforces monotonic window-local onsets and prevents duplicate
same-instrument/same-onset loops rather than silently truncating them.
Inadequate probability mass on valid tokens is an explicit error.
Bounded peak normalization and overlapping context improve quiet-hit
recognition; velocities are compensated for the applied input gain.
Release-only windows without a new transient are not amplified into
spurious events.

The separately downloaded model is published by the original author:
https://huggingface.co/Pierfrancesco/adt-str
The original repository's README states that this work is CC-BY-SA-4.0.
Model revision: a33c5c6b191a4ca1e0f6dc22140947485eb36ce8, setting-tau-0.8.

This license applies to this component, not to independent Track2stem
code or other third-party dependencies. Preserve this attribution and
the ShareAlike terms when distributing adapted versions of this work.
